                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "0214e826-a3f5-4fb9-ada6-38dd15ea2e14",
                        "entry_id": "c6ab2891-4b86-3b9c-b212-131002e899c0",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "hounskulls"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d7bb935f-457e-366d-9747-d9de48fbd304",
                        "entry_id": "c6ab2891-4b86-3b9c-b212-131002e899c0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A type of visor, drawn out into a conical point like a muzzle or beak which improved ventilation and deflected blows, or a helmet having such a visor."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3fdccef4-7357-4329-9faa-5d8bb7ddb0e6",
                                "sense_id": "d7bb935f-457e-366d-9747-d9de48fbd304",
                                "text": "On the counter is a hounskull with aventail (a visored bascinet with mail tippet) with a small plume on the apex. A pair of bell-cuffed gauntlets and an arming sword hang outside."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f2745262-6c5f-473f-b7ad-fcfd77e68d27",
                                "sense_id": "d7bb935f-457e-366d-9747-d9de48fbd304",
                                "text": "The big helmets that might have given many knights claustrophobia were gradually abolished for “hounskulls”, close-fitting steel caps with pointed visors that could be flicked open for easier breathing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d8c63c25-a751-4058-99a8-f2b362a49ee8",
                                "sense_id": "d7bb935f-457e-366d-9747-d9de48fbd304",
                                "text": "The most characteristic form of visor was the so-called “hounskull,” which featured a pointed snout that helped to deflect weapons, as well as giving the wearer an intimidating, bestial look; other visors had a rounded face."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2c1959bc-b3a3-49f0-9cbf-7844532e5199",
                                "sense_id": "d7bb935f-457e-366d-9747-d9de48fbd304",
                                "text": "Others showed signs of traumatic impact: a hounskull bascinet, split across the snout as if by an axe; a piece of chainmail, smashed breast to waist by a lance or a spiked mace."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7e29a095-606e-41b0-b203-b09e615ceaa2",
                                "sense_id": "d7bb935f-457e-366d-9747-d9de48fbd304",
                                "text": "There were knights everywhere, all around him a chaos of ghastly pointed hounskulls, a kaleidoscope of crosses and coats of arms on shields, a hurricane of flashing swords, a maelstrom of horses' teeth, chests and hooves."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
